{%- comment -%}
  Giscus comments, only once the repo is fully configured (see `giscus:` in _config.yml),
  so a half-configured site never shows al-folio's "misconfigured" warning to readers.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% if site.plugins contains 'al_comments' and page.giscus_comments and site.giscus.repo_id and site.giscus.category_id %}
  <section class="article-comments" id="comments">
    <div class="site-section__head">
      <span class="site-index">//</span>
      <h2>Discussion</h2>
      <p>Questions, corrections and ideas are welcome. Comments use GitHub Discussions, so you'll need a GitHub account.</p>
    </div>
    {% include plugins/al_comments.liquid %}
  </section>
{% endif %}
